# =============================================================================
# What is excluded from version control inside simulations/
#
# The folder itself IS versioned (the root .gitignore no longer lists it). It is
# kept out of the built package by ^simulations$ in .Rbuildignore, which is a
# separate mechanism and is unaffected.
# =============================================================================

# Per-replication output: ~315 MB and fully regenerable. Every (study, condition)
# derives a deterministic L'Ecuyer-CMRG stream from SIM_BASE_SEED in R/00_config.R,
# so any condition re-runs bit-for-bit. The aggregated CSVs -- the shipped result --
# are NOT ignored.
data/raw/

# Published papers. Excluded to avoid redistributing copyrighted PDFs from a
# repository that may become public. Kept on disk; cite them, do not commit them.
papers/

# RA-facing onboarding and task sheets. Excluded by request.
students/

# Re-include the legacy archive. The root .gitignore has a global `archive/` rule
# aimed at the repository-root archive/, which catches this one collaterally.
# simulations/archive/ is the documented record of the pre-rebuild defects and is
# cited by line number in README.md and SOURCE-VERIFICATION.md, so it is versioned.
!archive/

# Re-include the results viewer. The root .gitignore's bare `app` rule (aimed at the
# repository-root app/) matches a directory named `app` at ANY depth, so it would
# otherwise silently drop the whole Shiny programme -- app.R, www/ and the
# design-alternatives/ mockups -- from version control.
!app/

# NB app/rsconnect/shinyapps.io/ebiact/simulations.dcf is therefore versioned too.
# It holds no credentials (account name, app id, public URL only) and is what lets
# rsconnect::deployApp() redeploy to the existing app instead of creating a new one.
